# Meshing & solver automation notes

##Meshing notes

In openFOAM 2412 wsl, i have been trying to mesh DrivAER model with the references from "https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0167610524000746#sec3".

"https://gitlab.com/openfoam/core/openfoam/-/tree/OpenFOAM-v2412?ref_type=tags"

All the openFOAM operations have been done with opeFOAM pre loaded in the bash file, if this is not hte case this has to be done before running every operation or add include the command in the bash run files.

Geometry has been imported to blender and stls have been created for the domain without the tire holes at contact patch and exported in ascii batch mode with 1000 scale (in mm).

In openFOAM case directory symlinks have been created in "constat/triSurface" for the stls included.
Inorder to do this with ease, use "for f in source/directory/path/*.stl; do ln -s "$f" target/directory/constant/triSurface/; done" - "for f in ../../../stlGeometry/stlExport/*.stl; do ln -s "$f" ../triSurface/; done"

Created a bash file (bounds_extractor.sh) that calculates the min & max values and write to blockMesh.

The cell sizes are also tuned for the sake of saving my pc from breaking it's back.

Running "blockMesh" should create a basic background mesh with all the above steps followed


SnappyHexMesh has been partly inspired by "https://www.wolfdynamics.com/wiki/meshing_OF_SHM.pdf" and my master thesis at Scania.

"master_bash.sh" is the master bash file to run the whole snappy hex mesh.

Attempteting to decompose the mesh and reconstruct.


"https://gitlab-hpc.cineca.it/exafoam/spuma/-/blob/develop/src/parallel/decompose/kahipDecomp/Make/files?ref_type=heads"  Kahip decomposition for effectiveness.
Decomposed with 2 cores cause of my potato pc.

Followed by snappyHexMesh in parallel (this can be avoided with serial) with -overwrite flag.

This mesh is then later reconstructed, renumberes and scale the mesh to meters using transformPoints and -scale flag.

In the process of refiening, the DrivAER body has been scaled (4 2 2) with more emphasis on the flow direction and has been transformed and used as a refinementSurface (boi).

The inlet outlet symmetry has been reduced in max refinement to better match the farfield flow away from the body.

All systems working now, upuntil volume mesh and the next step will be trying to run a solver and get priliminary results and map the required results.

